# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: report
# board: only
# A report on demand: what the shell holds, asked for by a signal.
#
# Nothing has gone wrong here.  A person who wants to know what the
# desk thinks it has -- which boards, which programs, a run under way
# -- sends SIGUSR2 from a terminal and reads a file.  The signal only
# asks; the loop writes, on its next turn, so the snapshot is read by
# the one thread that may read it.
wait 60
note first, About this system: one row for all of this, the newest
note report, which a click opens -- in whatever opens text here, or
note failing that the folder it is in, since a fresh machine registers
note nothing.  A report is asked for so that there is one to name.
report
wait 30
click 20 8
wait 4
menu-pick About this system
wait 10
expect-title About this system
click 470 287
wait 40
expect-title reports
key w cmd
wait 10
click-window About this system
wait 4
key Escape
wait 10
click 980 30
wait 10
menu-pick Programming
wait 10
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 250
expect-title Project
report
wait 60
note the file names the mounted board, with its port
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_reports/latest-report.txt /devices/tiku
note and the program that is talking to the desk
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_reports/latest-report.txt TikuBasic
note and what asked for it
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_reports/latest-report.txt asked for: SIGUSR2
note the trail is in it too, with the launch that just happened
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_reports/latest-report.txt launch TikuBasic
note and the desk knows it wrote one
expect-read trail:report report written
quit
